{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>has known a man</b> — in gematria: her virginity does not return." "<b>has known</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: דיבש גלעד and נפלאים מעשיך ונפשי יודעת מאד. And this is what is stated in Yevamot, that they passed them before the Tzitz: all whose face turns green — it is known that she was violated. And that is נפלאים מעשיך — for through the wonders of Your deeds it becomes known whether she is יודעת איש." "<b>and every woman who has known a man licontly</b> — in gematria: if she is a girl of three years and one day." "<b>and not a man was missing from us</b> — in gematria: לעבירות."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:31.213379349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}